<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: New IBM plant to generate 2,000 jobs in Ireland.</title>
<headline>New IBM plant to generate 2,000 jobs in Ireland.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Information technology company IBM will create in excess of 2,000 jobs in Ireland when it sets up a new 150 million Irish pounds plant in west Dublin, Irish media said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>Earlier this year IBM announced it was setting up a 750-job Telecentre in Dublin, about 300 of the positions have already been filled.</p>
<p>Currently IBM is on the point of establishing a major plant in west Dublin in one of the biggest projects ever announced in Ireland.</p>
<p>The plant, which will include manufacturing and a range of other services, will represent an investment of at least 150 million, reports said.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9775</p>
